# Cursor follows .gitignore and its own default list (lock files, .env*, node_modules, pictures, film, sound) by itself;
# this file adds to that. A line hides a path from Cursor's Agent, Tab, @-mentions and index; a line with "!" brings one
# back. Not a lock: Cursor's terminal and MCP tools still reach everything (https://cursor.com/docs/reference/ignore-file).

# Secrets: also in .gitignore, repeated so that Cursor's Agent never reads them even if .gitignore changes
.env*
private/
*.pem
.vercel/

# assets/ is ignored by Git, so Cursor skips it entirely. Its small text (receipts, proof descriptions, generation
# records, prompts: about 6 MB) should be findable, its media (about 9 GB) should not: bring the folder back, hide
# everything in it again, then bring back only text. Cursor's docs promise "!" against .gitignore, not against a
# folder .gitignore excludes as a whole; check in a chat that @assets/proofs/fler-rum/proof.json is offered.
!assets/
assets/**
!assets/**/
!assets/**/*.json
!assets/**/*.txt
!assets/**/*.md

# Library code that is not the project's own and is far too long to read: the three.js library as it was brought in with
# the card material study, and the two built pages of that study (each is three.js plus about 300 lines of ours, packed
# by webpack). They are used as they are and never edited; the study's own source is materials/source/src/.
materials/kortmaterial.js
materials/markermaterial.js
materials/source/references/card-materials/vendor/three.module.js
